# A 21MB x86_64 Mach-O binary that nothing in the spec, the requirements, the
# README or install mentions. Swept in by a `git add -A` in b0d65e0. Left on
# disk, out of the build.
bin/tirith

# The skill curator's own bookmark: when it last ran, how long it took. Written
# by the agent on every pass, so tracking it makes every run a diff.
skills/.curator_state

# The scheduler's own bookkeeping, swept in by the same `git add -A` as the rest.
# Nothing in the repo reads either of them. Only .jobs files belong under cron/,
# and two of the three are rendered by bin/render so they are ignored above.
cron/usage_audit.jsonl
cron/catch_up_occurrences
cron/jobs.json
cron/executions.db
cron/output/
cron/.fire-*.lock
cron/.jobs.lock
cron/.tick.lock

# The age private key opens deploy/secrets/claude-credentials.json.age, which is
# committed. Both in one repo is the same as committing the plaintext. The key
# lives in ~/.config/hermes/age-key.txt and on the platform as a secret.
age-key.txt
hermes-age-key.txt
*.age.key
*age-key*.txt
.clean_shutdown

